  clock: 4  # c16a
  nonce: c16a  # c16a
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #244 (dev 9b0682fbaf), on behavioral evidence, not a proxy.\n\nRepro re-run on the merged tree, all four arms:\n  from decoy_lib import open -> v.read()   tagged 1 -> 0   (the FP, closed)\n  plain open(p) -> v.read()   (control)    tagged 2 -> 2   (non-destruction asserted)\n  from pathlib import Path -> .replace()   tagged 1 -> 1   (TP preserved)\n  from fastapi import Path -> .replace()   tagged 1 -> 0   (forecast FP, closed)\n\nThe last two require adding Path to EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES, as the original\nfiling's measurement did; they pin the future receiver-typing case rather than a\npresent-day one, and are labelled as such in the test.\n\nFIXED AT THE PRODUCER, not the consumer: _external_constructor_module's ast.Name\nbranch now routes through the new _import_binding_for predicate, which\n_receiver_type_id_trustworthy (WI-supat D3) also consumes -- it already had the\nidentical test inline. No consumer changed; lookup_with_module, gate_named_entry\nand taint._lookup_named_entry are untouched and correct as written.\n\nTHE FILED REMEDY IS WITHDRAWN, not deferred. See the rewritten description for\nthe 8-repo A/B (61.5%-87.2% of reported boundaries destroyed, zero gained).\n\nCAVEAT ON THIS CLOSURE: the corpus delta is 0 boundaries in either direction\ntoday (330 bare open() sites across 5 Python repos, 0 import-shadowed, three\npositive controls proving the shadow detectors fire). So the invariant holds and\nthe FP is closed, but no cohort-level improvement is claimed and none should be\nattributed to this PR. The value is the removed FP plus the guard on the 467\nbare Path() sites that receiver-typing work will walk into.\n\nNOT verified: whether any taint FINDING moves. The matcher was measured\n(hint pathlib.Path -> host_fs sink; hint external -> None) but no taint BFS or\nverify-claims run was done."  # c16a
